warp|bend-out-of-shape|VERB|Bend out of shape|To become bent or twisted from the original shape, or cause this change.|cong vênh; làm cong vênh|Moisture warped the wooden lid until it no longer fitted the box.|Độ ẩm làm nắp gỗ cong vênh đến mức nó không còn vừa với hộp.|Transitive moisture warps wood or intransitive wood warps. Warped and warping are regular forms.|-
including|with-as-part-of-the-group|PREPOSITION|With as part of the group|Used to name someone or something that forms part of a larger group or total.|bao gồm; kể cả|Eight people joined the walk, including two new members.|Tám người tham gia chuyến đi bộ, trong đó có hai thành viên mới.|Including plus noun phrase; the named items are within the total, not additional to it.|0
noble|morally-admirable|ADJECTIVE|Morally admirable|Showing admirable qualities such as generosity, courage or a concern for others.|cao quý; cao thượng|Sharing the limited water with strangers was a noble act.|Chia sẻ lượng nước ít ỏi với người lạ là một hành động cao thượng.|A noble act or aim; nobly is the adverb. This meaning does not require aristocratic status.|0
noble|aristocratic-status|ADJECTIVE|Aristocratic status|Belonging to a hereditary high social rank.|thuộc giới quý tộc|The novel follows a noble family living in an isolated castle.|Tiểu thuyết kể về một gia đình quý tộc sống trong lâu đài biệt lập.|Usually before a noun; noble family, noble birth. Social status does not imply moral goodness.|1
noble|aristocratic-person|NOUN|Aristocratic person|A person belonging to a hereditary high social rank.|người thuộc giới quý tộc|Several nobles attended the fictional royal ceremony.|Một số quý tộc dự buổi lễ hoàng gia hư cấu.|Countable; a noble, nobles. Nobleman and noblewoman are related gender-specific words.|-
therefore|logical-result|ADVERB|Logical result|For that reason, or as a result of what has been stated.|vì vậy; do đó|The gate was locked; therefore, we used the side entrance.|Cổng đã khóa; vì vậy, chúng tôi dùng lối vào bên cạnh.|Connecting adverb; use a full stop or semicolon between independent clauses. It is not normally a coordinating conjunction like and.|0
want|desire-something|VERB|Desire something|To wish to have something or to do something.|muốn; mong muốn|I want a quieter place to read this afternoon.|Tôi muốn một chỗ yên tĩnh hơn để đọc sách chiều nay.|Want plus noun or to-infinitive; want to read. Usually a state verb rather than a progressive action.|0
want|wish-another-person-to-act|VERB|Wish another person to act|To wish that another person would do something.|muốn ai làm gì|They want the carpenter to build a lower shelf.|Họ muốn người thợ mộc làm một ngăn kệ thấp hơn.|Want someone to do something; do not normally use want that someone does something.|1
